Killed by an orc

Decided to try a Priest for a change from my usual Knight/Ranger
recently. Two nice starting books (+Healing and +DetectObjects) proved
to be quite useful for finding my way about without getting hideously
maimed, and my pet kitten called Master Sprinkles was no slouch either.
Some hard shoes were kindly donated by a passing peaceful dwarf who had
a disagreement with Master Sprinkles. Two early shops and vaults both
cleaned out, and price-ID'd many useful scrolls (including blessed
charging!). Also sold the shopkeepers back some of their own goods for
that little extra ^_^ Managed to level up on Mace and Dart (plenty of
these lying around thanks to a kobold invasion) and could quickly
dispatch most of the worst nasties I encountered. There were a few
panicky moments (nymphs stealing my food while I was hungry and heading
for a safe corner to eat, a whole swarm of snakes suddenly crowding
into the room where I was busy stowing stuff in a box) but nothing
life-threatening. At one point, I got tele-trapped in a vault with no
digging utilities, but luckily I got desperate enough to read
unidentified scrolls, one of which was ?Teleport (the previous one was
?ConfuseMonster, which came in handy when I teleported straight into a
fight with a Gnomish wizard). Poor Master Sprinkles got killed by a
kobold, after which I declared a vendetta against all 'k', and swore to
blessed-genocide them all once I got the means.

Then came the throne room. Just a little tiny one, with about 6
monsters, all swiftly dispatched; including a kobold lord: "Vengeance
for Master Sprinkles!". I stored my gold and some crucial items in a
handily-nearby box and did a little #sit.

	You may wish for an object

Oh yeah, baby. I did some serious thinking and weighing-up of options.
I'd already landed myself a [CloakProtection, so I decided against the
GreyDSM (I know it's not the same thing, but good enough for low-level
characters). Had yet to acquire poison resistance (despiting stuffing
myself to satiation with every darn spider, scorpion and centipede in
sight!), so gave serious thought to GreenDSM. A nice shiny weapon would
also be nice, but I only get one shot at this. I eventually decided on
SilverDSM, as I'm not very good at Sokoban, and didn't like to cheat at
it (which wouldn't be very appropriate for a Lawful Priest anyway).

Okay. Throne does its thing, I get the SDSM. Collect my stuff and a few
gems that are lying around. Try writing with a few; one is a hard
stone! I joyously skip down the (lighted) corridor and find a white
unicorn prancing about! Okay, Mr Unicorn, just stand still for a
second, and I'll give you this shiny stone! Oh, lookit pretty! He
dodges my advances and vanishes; he's beside a (dark) corridor
entrance, so I'm not certain if he's 'ported or just run off. I
carefully walk down the corridor to find out... and am promptly kicked
in the face by a BLACK unicorn. Honestly, this is just silly. I'm still
below max HP from the throne-room fight earlier, and ended up slow
after it too (carrying too much probably doesn't help). Well, no great
problem; just lock the door on the unicorns, go stash some stuff and
heal up.

Well, at this point I realise that there were down-stairs in the black
unicorn's room. There are also down-stairs over here; it's the Mines
branch! I decide to take on the Mines before coming back to deal with
Pointy Head back there; a few more levels never hurts when fighting a
unicorn, after all. There's an altar on the floor above me, so I should
be able to lug him up there for a rather nice sacrificial offering,
which Tyr should be happy about; I'm hoping it will get me a special
gift! I stash my rather heavy wallet (I can come back for it after I
clear up Minetown a little) and some unidentified cursed potions I'd
rather not have about my person just now thankyouverymuch. Now
unencumbered, I head down into the Mines and start carving a path
through the Gnomes, who I don't like very much on account of a nasty
run-in with a Gnomish wizard earlier (yes, another one). Goes pretty
well, I find mucho goodies and stash them in a corner; engrave-ID'ing a
wand provides digging, so I carve the E-word into the stash square for
good measure. The next level goes much the same, and I lug some of the
loot upstairs to pile it all on one stash square for easy access.

	That's when I spot the orcs.

There are quite a few of them swarming towards me along the corridor.
No problem, I can dispatch these. THWANG goes my dart. THWANG goes a
poisoned dart back at me. Uh-oh, this isn't going according to plan. I
back up to the wall as they enter skull-bashing range and start
swinging my mace left, right, and centre. THUNK Gaargh! THUNK Gaargh!
THUNK ... you get the picture. Orcs are dropping like the proverbial
flies, but I'm still surrounded on 4 sides!

	The orc drinks a brown potion. The orc seems to be moving faster.

I decide to throw caution to the wind; ZAP goes a wand I haven't
identified yet. It's a wand of striking! Much excitement ensues. Of
course, the orcs are still hitting me; it's at this point I realise I
haven't been watching my HP closely enough since that guy became fast.
He must have a blessed scimitar or something as well (don't laugh, orcs
do occasionally get them!) because I am far too low to be healthy. Cast
healing, sharpish!

	You fail to cast the spell correctly.

Oh no. Fungus-for-brains and his chums whack another boatload of HP off
me. A quick survey of the inventory reveals nothing potentially useful.
Not even an unidentified scroll, potion, or wand; I've dumped all those
on my stash square, which is about a quarter of a screen too far away
to help me now! I could try to #pray, but I haven't been sacrificing
much of late, and the last thing I need is to get in Tyr's bad books
right now. My failure rate on +Healing is only very small, I should be
able to do it!

	You fail to cast the spell correctly. The orc hits. The orc hits!
	You die...
	DYWYPI?

Oh well. It was nice while it lasted. Time for a new Priest,
methinks...



